<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Slides on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/slides/</link><description>Recent content in Slides on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 12 Feb 2010 12:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/slides/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Le Mans 1968</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/le-mans-1986/</link><pubDate>Fri, 12 Feb 2010 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/le-mans-1986/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 13 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 20 links are now broken — mostly deleted or made-private Flickr photos, dead Flickr &lt;code&gt;farmN&lt;/code&gt; subdomains, and defunct feed-syndication infrastructure. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m in the process of scanning in some of my Dad&amp;rsquo;s old slides and I came across a selection he took from his visit to Le Mans in 1968, two years before I was born.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s what I&amp;rsquo;ve scanned so far, can&amp;rsquo;t wait to see what else is in the slide box labeled &amp;ldquo;Le Mans Sept 1968&amp;rdquo;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4347151880/" title="Le Mans 1968 IMG_0081 by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4005/4347151880_063c65ba40.jpg" width="500" height="327" alt="Le Mans 1968 IMG_0081" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4346406855/" title="Le Mans 1968 IMG_0082 by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2725/4346406855_1ebd1895db.jpg" width="500" height="324" alt="Le Mans 1968 IMG_0082" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;